    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "247ba792_89b101bd",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/notedb/RepoSequence.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T22:29:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is wrong: the logic of using the `refs/sequences/*` ref is:\n- Set the current value in `counter`\n- Allocate a batch of `batchSize` and set the new `limit`\n- Update the `refs/sequences/*` ref with the `counter` + `batchSize`\n\nHowever, here we set on `refs/sequences/*` the *same* value that we have in `counter` and still we consider the `batchSize` allocated.\n\nIt then leaves the in-memory counter and ref on `refs/sequences/*` in an inconsistent state: the batch allocated isn\u0027t reflected on the repository, causing potential duplication of change numbers.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 308,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 308,
        "endChar": 71
      },
